await tools.progress.append_progress({content: "STAGE 2 — goal: fix three distinct coupling sites. read: no file access permitted (read/glob denied, empty workdir); relied on the scope contract text. observed: contract lists assignment/Sinkhorn, hierarchy, residual/transition as suggested positions, implying other agents will take those; also mentions 'inherited unused hyperbolic code' as a non-qualifier. reasoning: choose three sites not on the suggested list — (A) the straight-through backward path, (B) the atom-position/shape parameterisation (behaviour-derived radial shells), (C) the reconstruction target (gyro-barycentre). open: write full specs with derived constants and frozen-scale costs."});
await tools.progress.append_progress({content: "STAGE 3 — IDEA A result (GEO-STE-GATE). Coupling: gradient returned by the STE is w_b(i)*(lambda_p/lambda_u)*gyr[u,-p](g_u); behaviour = standardised out-transition entropy from training split; geometry = conformal factor + gyration of the Poincare ball. Removal of either changes the update, hence the SID assignment. Cost: O(B d) per step, <1% Stage2. Distinct because geometry sits in the backward pass, not in a loss or an assignment cost."});
await tools.progress.append_progress({content: "STAGE 4 — IDEA B result (GEO-SHELL-RQ). Coupling: atom radius r_lg = (N-B_g)/(N+B_g) from measured hierarchical branching of the training transition graph, fed into m = exp_0((2/sqrt(c)) artanh(sqrt(c) r) u_hat), atoms e = exp_m(eps). Radius is derived (Sarkar embedding of a tree with B_g leaves), no tuned constant. Cost: one-off precompute plus O(K L d) projection per step."});
await tools.progress.append_progress({content: "STAGE 5 — IDEA C result (GYRO-TARGET-RQ). Coupling: reconstruction target b_i = exp_{p_i}(eta_i * mean_j log_{p_i}(sg(p_j))), eta_i = c_i/(1+c_i) from measured top-1 successor probability, successors = immediate next items in training sessions only. Changing either term changes what the encoder is asked to encode, hence the SID. Cost: O(E d) refresh once per epoch, ~0 marginal per step. Risk: identity smoothing, bounded by eta<=1/2."});
return "ok";

