input.code:
await tools.progress.append_progress({content: "STAGE 6 — FINAL ANSWER (summary of the three delivered ideas; full text printed in the reply).

IDEA 1 GEO-STE-GATE: curved straight-through. dL/dz_e(i) = [1+tanh((H_out(i)-mu_H)/sigma_H)] * (lambda^c_phat/lambda^c_u) * gyr[u,-phat](g_u). Behaviour = training-split out-transition entropy (frozen offline table, val/test never read). Geometry = Poincare conformal factors + gyration in the STE. Cost O(B d)/step, <0.5% Stage2. Ablations: gate=1; transport=identity/Euclidean.

IDEA 2 GEO-SHELL-RQ: behaviour-branching radial shells. e_{l,k}=exp_{m}(eps), m=exp_0((2/sqrt(c))artanh(sqrt(c)*(N-B_g)/(N+B_g))*u_hat), B_g = measured leaf mass of training-transition community g; per-step geodesic projection back into the shell. Constant is derived (Sarkar tree radius), nothing tuned. Cost: one-off tree+Frechet precompute, O(K L d) per step. Ablations: uniform shells (B_g=N/K); Euclidean radii/distance/arithmetic barycentre.

IDEA 3 GYRO-TARGET-RQ: curved reconstruction target. b_i=exp_{p_i}(eta_i * mean_{j in S_i} log_{p_i}(sg(p_j))), eta_i=c_i/(1+c_i), S_i = immediate successors from training sessions, c_i = measured top-1 transition probability. Both terms sit in the single target, so removing either changes what the encoder is fitted to. Cost O(E d) per epoch refresh, negligible per step. Ablations: eta=0 (plain AE); Euclidean mean and loss.

All three need exactly one training run, no sweep, no seed repeat; every constant is measured or closed-form. Distinct sites: backward pass, atom geometry, reconstruction target — deliberately not the assignment/Sinkhorn or extra-loss positions that the contract lists as examples."});
return "saved";

